/* ----------------------------- Data model ----------------------------- */
/*
 FUTURE ARCHITECTURE ROADMAP — DOCUMENTATION ONLY
 ------------------------------------------------
 Personal_Study_Library.html remains the MAIN STUDY BASE.

 Intended hierarchy:
   MAIN STUDY BASE
     -> SUBJECT WORKSPACE
       -> optional CHAPTER / UNIT grouping
         -> STUDY MODULE

 A STUDY MODULE is a self-contained, source-based study workspace rather than
 merely an uploaded file. A future module may contain its original source,
 Reader, Study Guide, Active Recall, Reveal Tables, Notes, MCQs, Progress,
 Weak Topics, bookmarks, annotations, and source/subject-specific tools.

 Important principles for future development:
 - Keep the outside/main library simple; detailed academic progress belongs
   inside subjects and modules, not on the root subject cards.
 - Every Study Module belongs to a subject and may optionally be grouped in a
   chapter/unit.
 - Uploading a source must preserve the original source. Future upload flow:
     Store as File  OR  Create Study Module.
 - Uploaded material is the PRIMARY academic source for module-generated tools.
 - Study Modules should be portable/self-contained and reuse a common
   STUDY MODULE ENGINE plus source/content data.
 - Different subjects can adapt the module toolset (for example calculations,
   diagrams, workflows, drug tables, etc.) without forcing every module to use
   every tool.
 - Private master data must never be sent to a recipient merely to be hidden in
   the browser; future sharing should deliver only an allow-listed payload.
 - Global calendar notes belong to the Main Base as organizational data; they are
   separate from module-specific study notes.
 - Chapter 25 remains a separate Study Module internally. In this Android-friendly build,
   its self-contained HTML is bundled only as a launchable module asset so content:// file
   restrictions do not break the connection between the Main Base and the module.

 This roadmap deliberately does NOT add a studyModules IndexedDB store yet.
 Keeping IndexedDB name/version/store structure unchanged avoids touching or
 resetting existing saved library data during this documentation update.
*/
const STUDY_ARCHITECTURE=Object.freeze({
 mainBase:'Personal_Study_Library.html',
 hierarchy:['Main Study Base','Subject Workspace','Optional Chapter / Unit','Study Module'],
 terminology:Object.freeze({sourceFile:'Source File',studyModule:'Study Module',moduleEngine:'Study Module Engine'}),
 studyModuleStatus:'roadmap-only',
 moduleCreationChoices:['Store as File','Create Study Module'],
 sourcePrinciple:'Preserve the original source and build study tools around it.',
 progressPrinciple:'Detailed progress stays inside subjects and study modules; keep the main library simple.',
 privacyPrinciple:'Shared clients should receive only explicitly allowed content, never the private master library.'
});
